{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Also.</b> On the day when there is light, he does not eat, but only in darkness. The meaning is that because of his many pursuits and his toil to gather money, he does not eat until nightfall, and he is full of anger and sickness of the soul, which is fear."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:47.632786380Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}